e learning. However, in response to an erroneous movement, the nervous system often engages a reflex that corrects for that error, thus expending time and energy. Here, we modulated this cost of error and found that increasing the cost increased how much the brain learned from error. Thus, the landscape of the loss associated with the act of correcting for error regulates the rates of sensorimotor learning.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1073\/pnas.2101717118","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2021,9,27]],"date-time":"2021-09-27T16:48:24Z","timestamp":1632761304000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1073\/pnas.cm10313","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":25,"title":["The cost of correcting for error during sensorimotor adaptation"],"prefix":"10.1073","volume":"118","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6732-1296","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Ehsan","family":"Sedaghat-Nejad","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Laboratory for Computational Motor Control, Department of Biomedical Engineering, Johns Hopkins School of Medicine, Baltimore, MD 21205"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-7686-2569","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Reza","family":"Shadmehr","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Laboratory for Computational Motor Control, Department of Biomedical Engineering, Johns Hopkins School of Medicine, Baltimore, MD 21205"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"341","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2021,9,27]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_3_4_1_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1073\/pnas.0308394101"},{"key":"e_1_3_4_2_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1152\/jn.00177.2012"},{"key":"e_1_3_4_3_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/nn.3956"},{"key":"e_1_3_4_4_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1152\/jn.00032.2014"},{"key":"e_1_3_4_5_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/s00221-017-